    "body": "## What\n\nA short table in `skills/sglang-explainer-video/references/pronunciation.md` for terms that fail `pron_check` with no passing respelling, and how the narration reworded them while the screen keeps the term.\n\n| Written | Whisper heard | Narration says instead |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| dstate | State | 状态维度 |\n| ncu | 看 | Nsight Compute |\n| swizzle | Swizo | 交错排列的内存布局 |\n\nPlus the OK~ terms from the same video to listen for on the render (warp/warps, grid, tile).\n\n## Why\n\nFound while building the PR 41223 / 41292 / 39680 explainer video (「改一行，为什么能快几倍？」). `pron_check --asr` printed FAIL with no respelling for all three; rewording the narration fixed them (0 issues on the recorded take). Recording the reword keeps the next video from hitting the same dead end.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
